From: Dmitry Afonchenko <undermove1@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 19:54:14 +0400
Subject: [PATCH 72/73] Meridian: switching to another profile's space in full
 screen stays in it

macOS put the other profile's window, shown over the full-screen one, into
a full screen Space of its own (a window that can be full screen, of an app
in full screen): every switch looked like a new window. Over a full-screen
window it is now auxiliary only, without tabbing; and a swapped window shows
on the Space on screen, not the one it was made on.

TestWindowState tells tests whether a window is shown, on the active Space
and where it is front to back.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01SwxrQ2eLfJ2bv8cCoG2va1
